hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1152","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, Bishr, meaning Ibn al-Mufaddal, told us. Imran, who is Ibn Muslim, told us, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would stand up to recite Tahajjud, he would say after saying “Allahu Akbar”: “O God, praise be to You.” You are the light of the heavens and the earth, and praise be to You, You are the establishment of the heavens and the earth, and praise be to You, You are the Lord of the heavens and the earth and whoever is in them, You are the Truth, Your word is true, your promise is true, meeting you is true, Paradise is true, Hell is true, and the Hour is true. Oh God, I submit to You, and in You I believe. In You I put my trust, and to You I repent, and to You I judge, and to You I dispute, and to You is my final return. O God, forgive me for what I have done, what I have delayed, and what I have pleased And I have not declared, “You are my God, there is no god but You.”"
